#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Un curso gratuito de IBM sobre información y computación cuántica"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inner products and projections"
msgstr "Productos internos y proyecciones"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr, operatorname */}\n"
"To better prepare ourselves to explore the capabilities and limitations of quantum circuits, we now introduce some additional mathematical concepts — namely the *inner product* between vectors (and its connection to the Euclidean norm), the notions of *orthogonality* and *orthonormality* for sets of vectors, and *projection* matrices, which will allow us to introduce a handy generalization of standard basis measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr, operatorname */}\n"
"Para prepararnos mejor y explorar las capacidades y limitaciones de los circuitos cuánticos, introducimos ahora algunos conceptos matemáticos adicionales: concretamente el *producto interno* entre vectores (y su conexión con la norma euclidiana), las nociones de *ortogonalidad* y *ortonormalidad* para conjuntos de vectores, y las matrices de *proyección*, que nos permitirán introducir una práctica generalización de las mediciones en base estándar.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Inner products {#inner-products}"
msgstr "Productos internos {#inner-products}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that when we use the Dirac notation to refer to an arbitrary column "
"vector as a ket, such as\n"
msgstr ""
"Recuerda que cuando usamos la notación de Dirac para referirnos a un vector "
"columna arbitrario como un ket, tal como\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"the corresponding bra vector is the *conjugate transpose* of this vector:\n"
msgstr ""
"el vector bra correspondiente es la *transpuesta conjugada* de ese vector:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively, if we have some classical state set $\\Sigma$ in mind, and we express a column vector as a ket,\n"
"such as\n"
msgstr ""
"Alternativamente, si tenemos en mente algún conjunto de estados clásicos $\\Sigma$ y expresamos un vector columna como un ket,\n"
"tal como\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "then the corresponding row (or bra) vector is the conjugate transpose\n"
msgstr ""
"entonces el vector fila (o bra) correspondiente es la transpuesta "
"conjugada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have that the product of a bra vector and a ket vector, viewed as matrices either having a single row or a single column, results in a scalar.\n"
"Specifically, if we have two column vectors\n"
msgstr ""
"También tenemos que el producto de un vector bra por un vector ket, vistos como matrices con una sola fila o una sola columna respectivamente, da como resultado un escalar.\n"
"Concretamente, si tenemos dos vectores columna\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{y}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "so that the row vector $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ is as in equation $(1),$ then\n"
msgstr ""
"de manera que el vector fila $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ es como en la ecuación "
"$(1),$ entonces\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\beta_1 + \\cdots + \\overline{\\alpha_n}\\beta_n.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\beta_1 + \\cdots + \\overline{\\alpha_n}\\beta_n.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, if we have two column vectors that we have written as\n"
msgstr "Alternativamente, si tenemos dos vectores columna escritos como\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{y}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "so that $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ is the row vector $(2),$ we find that\n"
msgstr ""
"de modo que $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ es el vector fila $(2),$ encontramos "
"que\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b\\rangle\\Biggr)\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_b \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b\\rangle\\Biggr)\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_b \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the last equality follows from the observation that $\\langle a \\vert"
" a \\rangle = 1$ and $\\langle a \\vert b \\rangle = 0$ for classical states"
" $a$ and $b$ satisfying $a\\neq b.$\n"
msgstr ""
"donde la última igualdad se sigue de la observación de que $\\langle a "
"\\vert a \\rangle = 1$ y $\\langle a \\vert b \\rangle = 0$ para estados "
"clásicos $a$ y $b$ que satisfacen $a\\neq b.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The value $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle$ is called the *inner product* between the vectors $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle.$\n"
"Inner products are critically important in quantum information and computation;\n"
"we would not get far in understanding quantum information at a mathematical level without them.\n"
msgstr ""
"El valor $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle$ se denomina el *producto interno* entre los vectores $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ y $\\vert \\phi \\rangle.$\n"
"Los productos internos son de una importancia crucial en la información y computación cuántica;\n"
"no llegaríamos muy lejos en la comprensión matemática de la información cuántica sin ellos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us now collect together some basic facts about inner products of "
"vectors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Reunamos ahora algunos hechos básicos sobre los productos internos de "
"vectores.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Relationship to the Euclidean norm.** The inner product of any vector\n"
msgstr ""
"**Relación con la norma euclidiana.** El producto interno de cualquier "
"vector\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   with itself is\n"
msgstr "   consigo mismo es\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\alpha_a\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert\\alpha_a\\vert^2\n"
"   = \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\alpha_a\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert\\alpha_a\\vert^2\n"
"   = \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Thus, the Euclidean norm of a vector may alternatively be expressed as\n"
msgstr ""
"   Así, la norma euclidiana de un vector puede expresarse alternativamente "
"como\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| = \\sqrt{ \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle }.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| = \\sqrt{ \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle }.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Notice that the Euclidean norm of a vector must always be a nonnegative real number.\n"
"   Moreover, the only way the Euclidean norm of a vector can be equal to zero is if every one of the entries is equal to zero, which is to say that the vector is the zero vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Observa que la norma euclidiana de un vector siempre debe ser un número real no negativo.\n"
"   Además, la única manera en que la norma euclidiana de un vector puede ser igual a cero es que todas sus entradas sean iguales a cero, es decir, que el vector sea el vector cero.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We can summarize these observations like this: for every vector $\\vert "
"\\psi \\rangle$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"   Podemos resumir estas observaciones de la siguiente manera: para todo "
"vector $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ tenemos\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   with $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$ if and only if $\\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0.$\n"
"   This property of the inner product is sometimes referred to as _positive definiteness_.\n"
msgstr ""
"   con $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$ si y solo si $\\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0.$\n"
"   Esta propiedad del producto interno se conoce a veces como _definición positiva_.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Conjugate symmetry.** For any two vectors\n"
msgstr "**Simetría conjugada.** Para cualesquiera dos vectores\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   \\quad\\text{y}\\quad\n"
"   \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   we have\n"
msgstr "   tenemos\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\beta_a} \\alpha_a,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a\n"
"   \\quad\\text{y}\\quad\n"
"   \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\beta_a} \\alpha_a,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   and therefore\n"
msgstr "   y por lo tanto\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\overline{\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle} = \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\overline{\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle} = \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Linearity in the second argument (and conjugate linearity in the first).**\n"
"Let us suppose that $\\vert \\psi \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle,$ and $\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle$ are vectors and $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_2$ are complex numbers. If we define a new vector\n"
msgstr ""
"**Linealidad en el segundo argumento (y linealidad conjugada en el primero).**\n"
"Supongamos que $\\vert \\psi \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle$ y $\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle$ son vectores y que $\\alpha_1$ y $\\alpha_2$ son números complejos. Si definimos un nuevo vector\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\phi\\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\phi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\phi_2\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\phi\\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\phi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\phi_2\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   then\n"
msgstr "   entonces\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigl( \\alpha_1\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"   = \\alpha_1 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigl( \\alpha_1\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"   = \\alpha_1 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   That is to say, the inner product is _linear_ in the second argument.\n"
"   This can be verified either through the formulas above or simply by noting that matrix multiplication is linear in each argument (and specifically in the second argument).\n"
msgstr ""
"   Es decir, el producto interno es _lineal_ en el segundo argumento.\n"
"   Esto puede verificarse tanto a través de las fórmulas anteriores como simplemente notando que la multiplicación de matrices es lineal en cada argumento (y en particular en el segundo).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Combining this fact with conjugate symmetry reveals that the inner "
"product is _conjugate linear_ in the first argument. That is, if $\\vert "
"\\psi_1 \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,$ and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ "
"are vectors and $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_2$ are complex numbers, and we "
"define\n"
msgstr ""
"   Combinar este hecho con la simetría conjugada revela que el producto "
"interno es _conjugado lineal_ en el primer argumento. Es decir, si $\\vert "
"\\psi_1 \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle$ y $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ son "
"vectores y $\\alpha_1$ y $\\alpha_2$ son números complejos, y definimos\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\bigl( \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\bigr)\n"
"   \\vert\\phi\\rangle\n"
"   = \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert \\phi \\rangle + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\phi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\bigl( \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\bigr)\n"
"   \\vert\\phi\\rangle\n"
"   = \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert \\phi \\rangle + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\phi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The Cauchy–Schwarz inequality.**\n"
"For every choice of vectors $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ having the same number of entries, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"**La desigualdad de Cauchy–Schwarz.**\n"
"Para toda elección de vectores $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ y $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ con el mismo número de entradas, tenemos\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\vert \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\bigr| \\leq \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| \\bigl\\| \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   \\bigr\\|.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\vert \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\bigr| \\leq \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| \\bigl\\| \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   \\bigr\\|.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   This is an incredibly handy inequality that gets used quite extensively "
"in quantum information (and in many other topics of study).\n"
msgstr ""
"   Esta es una desigualdad increíblemente útil que se emplea con mucha "
"frecuencia en información cuántica (y en muchos otros campos de estudio).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Orthogonal and orthonormal sets {#orthogonal-and-orthonormal-sets}"
msgstr ""
"Conjuntos ortogonales y ortonormales {#orthogonal-and-orthonormal-sets}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two vectors $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ are said to "
"be *orthogonal* if their inner product is zero:\n"
msgstr ""
"Se dice que dos vectores $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ y $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ "
"son *ortogonales* si su producto interno es cero:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Geometrically, we can think about orthogonal vectors as vectors at right "
"angles to each other.\n"
msgstr ""
"Geométricamente, podemos pensar en los vectores ortogonales como vectores "
"que forman ángulos rectos entre sí.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A set of vectors $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is called an *orthogonal set* if every vector in the set is orthogonal to every other vector in the set.\n"
"That is, this set is orthogonal if\n"
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de vectores $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ se denomina *conjunto ortogonal* si cada vector del conjunto es ortogonal a todos los demás vectores del conjunto.\n"
"Es decir, este conjunto es ortogonal si\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle = 0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle = 0\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for all choices of $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ for which $j\\neq k.$\n"
msgstr "para toda elección de $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ tal que $j\\neq k.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A set of vectors $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is called an *orthonormal* set if it is an orthogonal set and, in addition, every vector in the set is a unit vector.\n"
"Alternatively, this set is an orthonormal set if we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de vectores $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ se denomina *ortonormal* si es un conjunto ortogonal y, además, cada vector del conjunto es un vector unitario.\n"
"Alternativamente, este conjunto es ortonormal si se cumple\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & j = k\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & j\\neq k\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & j = k\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & j\\neq k\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for all choices of $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}.$\n"
msgstr "para toda elección de $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, a set $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is an *orthonormal basis* if, in addition to being an orthonormal set, it forms a basis.\n"
"This is equivalent to $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ being an orthonormal set and $m$ being equal to the dimension of the space from which $\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ are drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Finalmente, un conjunto $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ es una *base ortonormal* si, además de ser un conjunto ortonormal, forma una base.\n"
"Esto equivale a que $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ sea un conjunto ortonormal y que $m$ sea igual a la dimensión del espacio del que se toman $\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, for any classical state set $\\Sigma,$ the set of all standard "
"basis vectors\n"
msgstr ""
"Por ejemplo, para cualquier conjunto de estados clásicos $\\Sigma,$ el "
"conjunto de todos los vectores de la base estándar\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\big\\{ \\vert a \\rangle \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\big\\{ \\vert a \\rangle \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is an orthonormal basis.\n"
"The set $\\{\\vert+\\rangle,\\vert-\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis for the $2$-dimensional space corresponding to a single qubit, and the Bell basis $\\{\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\phi^-\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis for the $4$-dimensional space corresponding to two qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"es una base ortonormal.\n"
"El conjunto $\\{\\vert+\\rangle,\\vert-\\rangle\\}$ es una base ortonormal para el espacio de dimensión $2$ correspondiente a un solo qubit, y la base de Bell $\\{\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\phi^-\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\}$ es una base ortonormal para el espacio de dimensión $4$ correspondiente a dos qubits.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Extending orthonormal sets to orthonormal bases {#extending-orthonormal-"
"sets-to-orthonormal-bases}"
msgstr ""
"Extensión de conjuntos ortonormales a bases ortonormales {#extending-"
"orthonormal-sets-to-orthonormal-bases}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ are vectors that live in an $n$-dimensional space, and assume moreover that $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal set.\n"
"Orthonormal sets are always linearly independent sets, so these vectors necessarily span a subspace of dimension $m.$\n"
"From this we conclude that $m\\leq n$ because the dimension of the subspace spanned by these vectors cannot be larger than the dimension of the entire space from which they're drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Supongamos que $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ son vectores que viven en un espacio de dimensión $n$, y supongamos además que $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ es un conjunto ortonormal.\n"
"Los conjuntos ortonormales son siempre conjuntos linealmente independientes, por lo que estos vectores generan necesariamente un subespacio de dimensión $m.$\n"
"De esto concluimos que $m\\leq n$, ya que la dimensión del subespacio generado por estos vectores no puede ser mayor que la dimensión del espacio completo del que se toman.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If it is the case that $m<n,$ then it is always possible to choose an additional $n-m$ vectors\n"
"$\\vert \\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ so that\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ forms an orthonormal basis.\n"
"A procedure known as the *Gram–Schmidt orthogonalization process* can be used to construct these vectors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si se da el caso de que $m<n,$ siempre es posible elegir $n-m$ vectores adicionales\n"
"$\\vert \\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ de modo que\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ forme una base ortonormal.\n"
"Un procedimiento conocido como el *proceso de ortonormalización de Gram–Schmidt* puede utilizarse para construir estos vectores.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Orthonormal sets and unitary matrices {#orthonormal-sets-and-unitary-"
"matrices}"
msgstr ""
"Conjuntos ortonormales y matrices unitarias {#orthonormal-sets-and-unitary-"
"matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Orthonormal sets of vectors are closely connected with unitary matrices.\n"
"One way to express this connection is to say that the following three statements are logically equivalent (meaning that they are all true or all false) for any choice of a square matrix $U$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Los conjuntos ortonormales de vectores están estrechamente relacionados con las matrices unitarias.\n"
"Una forma de expresar esta conexión es decir que las tres afirmaciones siguientes son lógicamente equivalentes (es decir, todas son verdaderas o todas son falsas) para cualquier elección de una matriz cuadrada $U$:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The matrix $U$ is unitary (that is, $U^{\\dagger} U = \\mathbb{I} = U "
"U^{\\dagger}$).\n"
msgstr ""
"La matriz $U$ es unitaria (es decir, $U^{\\dagger} U = \\mathbb{I} = U "
"U^{\\dagger}$).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The rows of $U$ form an orthonormal set.\n"
msgstr "Las filas de $U$ forman un conjunto ortonormal.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The columns of $U$ form an orthonormal set.\n"
msgstr "Las columnas de $U$ forman un conjunto ortonormal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This equivalence is actually pretty straightforward when we think about how matrix multiplication and the conjugate transpose work.\n"
"Suppose, for instance, that we have a $3\\times 3$ matrix like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta equivalencia es bastante directa cuando pensamos en cómo funcionan la multiplicación de matrices y la transpuesta conjugada.\n"
"Supongamos, por ejemplo, que tenemos una matriz $3\\times 3$ como esta:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The conjugate transpose of $U$ looks like this:\n"
msgstr "La transpuesta conjugada de $U$ es:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Multiplying the two matrices, with the conjugate transpose on the left-hand "
"side, gives us this matrix:\n"
msgstr ""
"Multiplicar las dos matrices, con la transpuesta conjugada a la izquierda, "
"nos da esta matriz:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\quad &=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\quad &=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "If we form three vectors from the columns of $U,$\n"
msgstr "Si formamos tres vectores a partir de las columnas de $U,$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_2\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_3\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_2\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_3\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "then we can alternatively express the product above as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"entonces podemos expresar el producto anterior de la siguiente manera:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Referring to the equation $(3),$ we now see that the condition that this "
"matrix is equal to the identity matrix is equivalent to the orthonormality "
"of the set "
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_3\\rangle\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Refiriéndonos a la ecuación $(3),$ vemos ahora que la condición de que esta "
"matriz sea igual a la matriz identidad es equivalente a la ortonormalidad "
"del conjunto "
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_3\\rangle\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This argument generalizes to unitary matrices of any size.\n"
"The fact that the rows of a matrix form an orthonormal basis if and only if the matrix is unitary then follows from the fact that a matrix is unitary if and only if its transpose is unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Este argumento se generaliza a matrices unitarias de cualquier tamaño.\n"
"El hecho de que las filas de una matriz formen una base ortonormal si y solo si la matriz es unitaria se sigue entonces del hecho de que una matriz es unitaria si y solo si su transpuesta también es unitaria.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the equivalence described above, together with the fact that every orthonormal set can be extended to form an orthonormal basis, we conclude the following useful fact:\n"
"Given any orthonormal set of vectors $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ drawn from an $n$-dimensional space, there exists a unitary matrix $U$ whose first $m$ columns are the vectors $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle.$\n"
"Pictorially, we can always find a unitary matrix having this form:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dada la equivalencia descrita anteriormente, junto con el hecho de que todo conjunto ortonormal puede extenderse para formar una base ortonormal, concluimos el siguiente hecho útil:\n"
"Dado cualquier conjunto ortonormal de vectores $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ tomados de un espacio de dimensión $n$, existe una matriz unitaria $U$ cuyas primeras $m$ columnas son los vectores $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle.$\n"
"Pictóricamente, siempre podemos encontrar una matriz unitaria de esta forma:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\left(\n"
"  \\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\\\\\n"
"    \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle & \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_m\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle &\n"
"    \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\n"
"  \\end{array}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\left(\n"
"  \\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\\\\\n"
"    \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle & \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_m\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle &\n"
"    \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\n"
"  \\end{array}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the last $n-m$ columns are filled in with any choice of vectors $\\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ that make\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ an orthonormal basis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí, las últimas $n-m$ columnas se completan con cualquier elección de vectores $\\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ que haga que\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ sea una base ortonormal.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Projections and projective measurements {#projections-and-projective-"
"measurements}"
msgstr ""
"Proyecciones y mediciones proyectivas {#projections-and-projective-"
"measurements}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Projection matrices {#projection-matrices}"
msgstr "Matrices de proyección {#projection-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A square matrix $\\Pi$ is called a *projection* if it satisfies two "
"properties:\n"
msgstr ""
"Una matriz cuadrada $\\Pi$ se llama *proyección* si satisface dos "
"propiedades:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Pi = \\Pi^{\\dagger}.$\n"
msgstr "$\\Pi = \\Pi^{\\dagger}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Pi^2 = \\Pi.$\n"
msgstr "$\\Pi^2 = \\Pi.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Matrices that satisfy the first condition — that they are equal to their own"
" conjugate transpose — are called *Hermitian matrices*, and matrices that "
"satisfy the second condition — that squaring them leaves them unchanged — "
"are called *idempotent* matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Las matrices que satisfacen la primera condición —es decir, que son iguales "
"a su propia traspuesta conjugada— se llaman *matrices hermitianas*, y las "
"matrices que satisfacen la segunda condición —que elevarlas al cuadrado las "
"deja sin cambios— se llaman matrices *idempotentes*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a word of caution, the word *projection* is sometimes used to refer to any matrix that satisfies just the second condition but not necessarily the first, and when this is done the term *orthogonal projection* is typically used to refer to matrices satisfying both properties.\n"
"In the context of quantum information and computation, however, the terms *projection* and *projection matrix* more typically refer to matrices satisfying both conditions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Como advertencia, la palabra *proyección* a veces se usa para referirse a cualquier matriz que satisface únicamente la segunda condición pero no necesariamente la primera; en ese caso, el término *proyección ortogonal* se emplea habitualmente para referirse a las matrices que satisfacen ambas propiedades.\n"
"Sin embargo, en el contexto de la información y la computación cuántica, los términos *proyección* y *matriz de proyección* se refieren con más frecuencia a matrices que satisfacen ambas condiciones.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "An example of a projection is the matrix\n"
msgstr "Un ejemplo de proyección es la matriz\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for any unit vector $\\vert \\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"We can see that this matrix is Hermitian as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"para cualquier vector unitario $\\vert \\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Podemos ver que esta matriz es hermitiana de la siguiente manera:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger} = \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\bigl( \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger} = \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\bigl( \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here, to obtain the second equality, we have used the formula\n"
msgstr "Aquí, para obtener la segunda igualdad, hemos usado la fórmula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(A B)^{\\dagger} = B^{\\dagger} A^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(A B)^{\\dagger} = B^{\\dagger} A^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which is always true, for any two matrices $A$ and $B$ for which the product"
" $AB$ makes sense.\n"
msgstr ""
"que siempre es válida para cualesquiera dos matrices $A$ y $B$ para las que "
"el producto $AB$ tenga sentido.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see that the matrix $\\Pi$ in $(4)$ is idempotent, we can use the assumption that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is a unit vector, so that it satisfies $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi\\rangle = 1.$\n"
"Thus, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ver que la matriz $\\Pi$ en $(4)$ es idempotente, podemos usar la hipótesis de que $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ es un vector unitario, de modo que satisface $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi\\rangle = 1.$\n"
"Por lo tanto, tenemos\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"= \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert \\bigr)^2\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"= \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert \\bigr)^2\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"More generally, if $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is any orthonormal set of vectors, then the matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"De manera más general, si $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ es cualquier conjunto ortonormal de vectores, entonces "
"la matriz\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{5}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{5}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is a projection.\n"
"Specifically, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"es una proyección.\n"
"En concreto, tenemos\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger}\n"
"&= \\biggl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\bigl(\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert\\bigr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"&= \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger}\n"
"&= \\biggl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\bigl(\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert\\bigr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"&= \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and\n"
msgstr "y\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"& = \\biggl( \\sum_{j = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{j = 1}^m\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert  \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"& = \\biggl( \\sum_{j = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{j = 1}^m\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert  \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the orthonormality of $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ implies the second-to-last equality.\n"
msgstr ""
"donde la ortonormalidad de $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ implica la penúltima igualdad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In fact, this exhausts all of the possibilities: *every* projection $\\Pi$ can be written in the form $(5)$ for some choice of an orthonormal set $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}.$\n"
"(Technically speaking, the zero matrix $\\Pi=0,$ which is a projection, is a special case.\n"
"To fit it into the general form $(5)$ we must allow the possibility that the sum is empty, resulting in the zero matrix.)\n"
msgstr ""
"De hecho, esto agota todas las posibilidades: *toda* proyección $\\Pi$ puede escribirse en la forma $(5)$ para alguna elección de un conjunto ortonormal $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}.$\n"
"(Técnicamente, la matriz cero $\\Pi=0,$ que es una proyección, es un caso especial.\n"
"Para encajarla en la forma general $(5)$ debemos permitir la posibilidad de que la suma sea vacía, lo que da como resultado la matriz cero.)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Projective measurements {#projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Mediciones proyectivas {#projective-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The notion of a measurement of a quantum system is more general than just standard basis measurements.\n"
"*Projective measurements* are measurements that are described by a collection of projections whose sum is equal to the identity matrix.\n"
"In symbols, a collection $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ of projection matrices describes a projective measurement if\n"
msgstr ""
"La noción de medición de un sistema cuántico es más general que las simples mediciones en la base estándar.\n"
"Las *mediciones proyectivas* son mediciones que se describen mediante una colección de proyecciones cuya suma es igual a la matriz identidad.\n"
"En símbolos, una colección $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ de matrices de proyección describe una medición proyectiva si\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When such a measurement is performed on a system $\\mathsf{X}$ while it is "
"in some state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ two things happen:\n"
msgstr ""
"Cuando se realiza dicha medición sobre un sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ mientras se "
"encuentra en algún estado $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ suceden dos cosas:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ the outcome of the measurement is $k$ "
"with probability equal to\n"
msgstr ""
"Para cada $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ el resultado de la medición es $k$ con"
" probabilidad igual a\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $k$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{el resultado es $k$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For whichever outcome $k$ the measurement produces, the state of "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Sea cual sea el resultado $k$ que produce la medición, el estado de "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ pasa a ser\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also choose outcomes other than $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ for projective measurements if we wish.\n"
"More generally, for any finite and nonempty set $\\Sigma,$ if we have a collection of projection matrices\n"
msgstr ""
"También podemos elegir resultados distintos de $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ para las mediciones proyectivas si lo deseamos.\n"
"De manera más general, para cualquier conjunto finito y no vacío $\\Sigma,$ si tenemos una colección de matrices de proyección\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_a:a\\in\\Sigma\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_a:a\\in\\Sigma\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "that satisfies the condition\n"
msgstr "que satisface la condición\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\Pi_a = \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\Pi_a = \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"then this collection describes a projective measurement whose possible "
"outcomes coincide with the set $\\Sigma,$ where the rules are the same as "
"before:\n"
msgstr ""
"entonces esta colección describe una medición proyectiva cuyos posibles "
"resultados coinciden con el conjunto $\\Sigma,$ donde las reglas son las "
"mismas que antes:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each $a\\in\\Sigma,$ the outcome of the measurement is $a$ with "
"probability equal to\n"
msgstr ""
"Para cada $a\\in\\Sigma,$ el resultado de la medición es $a$ con "
"probabilidad igual a\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $a$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{el resultado es $a$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For whichever outcome $a$ the measurement produces, the state of "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Sea cual sea el resultado $a$ que produce la medición, el estado de "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ pasa a ser\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, standard basis measurements are equivalent to projective measurements, where $\\Sigma$ is the set of classical states of whatever system $\\mathsf{X}$ we're talking about and our set of projection matrices is\n"
"$\\{\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert:a\\in\\Sigma\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Por ejemplo, las mediciones en la base estándar son equivalentes a mediciones proyectivas, donde $\\Sigma$ es el conjunto de estados clásicos del sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ del que estemos hablando y nuestro conjunto de matrices de proyección es\n"
"$\\{\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert:a\\in\\Sigma\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Another example of a projective measurement, this time on two qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}),$ is given by the set\n"
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\Pi_1\\},$ where\n"
msgstr ""
"Otro ejemplo de medición proyectiva, esta vez sobre dos qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}),$ lo da el conjunto\n"
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\Pi_1\\},$ donde\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\langle \\phi^+ \\vert + \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\langle \\phi^- \\vert + \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\langle \\psi^+ \\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\langle \\phi^+ \\vert + \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\langle \\phi^- \\vert + \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\langle \\psi^+ \\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{y}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we have multiple systems that are jointly in some quantum state and a "
"projective measurement is performed on just one of the systems, the action "
"is similar to what we had for standard basis measurements — and in fact we "
"can now describe this action in much simpler terms than we could before.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si tenemos múltiples sistemas que se encuentran conjuntamente en algún "
"estado cuántico y se realiza una medición proyectiva sobre solo uno de los "
"sistemas, la acción es similar a lo que teníamos para las mediciones en la "
"base estándar —y de hecho, ahora podemos describir esta acción en términos "
"mucho más simples que antes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be precise, let us suppose that we have two systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ in a quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ and a projective measurement described by a collection $\\{\\Pi_a : a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ is performed on the system $\\mathsf{X},$ while nothing is done to $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"Doing this is then equivalent to performing the projective measurement described by the collection\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ser más precisos, supongamos que tenemos dos sistemas $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ en un estado cuántico $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ y se realiza una medición proyectiva descrita por una colección $\\{\\Pi_a : a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ sobre el sistema $\\mathsf{X},$ mientras que no se hace nada sobre $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"Esto equivale a realizar la medición proyectiva descrita por la colección\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"on the joint system $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
"Each measurement outcome $a$ results with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"sobre el sistema conjunto $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
"Cada resultado de medición $a$ ocurre con probabilidad\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and conditioned on the result $a$ appearing, the state of the joint system "
"$(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"y condicionado a que aparezca el resultado $a,$ el estado del sistema "
"conjunto $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ pasa a ser\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{(\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{(\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Implementing projective measurements {#implementing-projective-measurements}"
msgstr ""
"Implementación de mediciones proyectivas {#implementing-projective-"
"measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Arbitrary projective measurements can be implemented using unitary "
"operations, standard basis measurements, and an extra workspace system, as "
"will now be explained.\n"
msgstr ""
"Las mediciones proyectivas arbitrarias pueden implementarse usando "
"operaciones unitarias, mediciones en la base estándar y un sistema de "
"espacio de trabajo adicional, como se explicará a continuación.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system and "
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ is a projective measurement on "
"$\\mathsf{X}.$ We can easily generalize this discussion to projective "
"measurements having different sets of outcomes, but in the interest of "
"convenience and simplicity we will assume the set of possible outcomes for "
"our measurement is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Supongamos que $\\mathsf{X}$ es un sistema y "
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ es una medición proyectiva sobre "
"$\\mathsf{X}.$ Podemos generalizar fácilmente esta discusión a mediciones "
"proyectivas con diferentes conjuntos de resultados, pero por conveniencia y "
"simplicidad asumiremos que el conjunto de posibles resultados de nuestra "
"medición es $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us note explicitly that $m$ is not necessarily equal to the number of "
"classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ — we'll let $n$ be the number of classical"
" states of $\\mathsf{X},$ which means that each matrix $\\Pi_k$ is an "
"$n\\times n$ projection matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Señalemos explícitamente que $m$ no es necesariamente igual al número de "
"estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{X}$ — denotaremos por $n$ el número de estados"
" clásicos de $\\mathsf{X},$ lo que significa que cada matriz $\\Pi_k$ es una"
" matriz de proyección de $n\\times n.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because we assume that $\\{\\Pi_0\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ represents a "
"projective measurement, it is necessarily the case that\n"
msgstr ""
"Dado que asumimos que $\\{\\Pi_0\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ representa una "
"medición proyectiva, necesariamente se cumple que\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\Pi_k = \\mathbb{I}_n.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\Pi_k = \\mathbb{I}_n.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our goal is to perform a process that has the same effect as performing this"
" projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X},$ but to do this using only unitary "
"operations and standard basis measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nuestro objetivo es realizar un proceso que tenga el mismo efecto que "
"realizar esta medición proyectiva sobre $\\mathsf{X},$ pero hacerlo usando "
"únicamente operaciones unitarias y mediciones en la base estándar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will make use of an extra workspace system $\\mathsf{Y}$ to do this, and specifically we'll take the classical state set of $\\mathsf{Y}$ to be $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ which is the same as the set of outcomes of the projective measurement.\n"
"The idea is that we will perform a standard basis measurement on $\\mathsf{Y},$ and interpret the outcome of this measurement as being equivalent to the outcome of the projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"We'll need to assume that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is initialized to some fixed state, which we'll choose to be $\\vert 0\\rangle.$\n"
"(Any other choice of fixed quantum state vector could be made to work, but choosing $\\vert 0\\rangle$ makes the explanation to follow much simpler.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Haremos uso de un sistema de espacio de trabajo adicional $\\mathsf{Y}$ para ello, y específicamente tomaremos el conjunto de estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{Y}$ como $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ que es el mismo que el conjunto de resultados de la medición proyectiva.\n"
"La idea es que realizaremos una medición en la base estándar sobre $\\mathsf{Y},$ e interpretaremos el resultado de esta medición como equivalente al resultado de la medición proyectiva sobre $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Necesitaremos asumir que $\\mathsf{Y}$ se inicializa en algún estado fijo, que elegiremos como $\\vert 0\\rangle.$\n"
"(Cualquier otra elección de vector de estado cuántico fijo podría funcionar, pero elegir $\\vert 0\\rangle$ hace que la explicación siguiente sea mucho más sencilla.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, in order for a standard basis measurement of $\\mathsf{Y}$ to tell us anything about $\\mathsf{X},$ we will need to allow $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ to interact somehow before measuring $\\mathsf{Y},$ by performing a unitary operation on the system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X}).$\n"
"First consider this matrix:\n"
msgstr ""
"Por supuesto, para que una medición en la base estándar de $\\mathsf{Y}$ nos diga algo sobre $\\mathsf{X},$ necesitaremos permitir que $\\mathsf{X}$ y $\\mathsf{Y}$ interactúen de alguna manera antes de medir $\\mathsf{Y},$ realizando una operación unitaria sobre el sistema $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X}).$\n"
"Primero consideremos esta matriz:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\Pi_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\Pi_k.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Expressed explicitly as a so-called *block matrix*, which is essentially a "
"matrix of matrices that we interpret as a single, larger matrix, $M$ looks "
"like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Expresada explícitamente como una llamada *matriz en bloques*, que es "
"esencialmente una matriz de matrices que interpretamos como una única matriz"
" más grande, $M$ tiene este aspecto:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, each $0$ represents an $n\\times n$ matrix filled entirely with zeros,"
" so that the entire matrix $M$ is an $nm\\times nm$ matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí, cada $0$ representa una matriz de $n\\times n$ rellena completamente "
"con ceros, de modo que la matriz completa $M$ es una matriz de $nm\\times "
"nm.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, $M$ is certainly not a unitary matrix (unless $m=1,$ in which case "
"$\\Pi_0 = \\mathbb{I},$ giving $M = \\mathbb{I}$ in this trivial case) "
"because unitary matrices cannot have any columns (or rows) that are entirely"
" $0;$ unitary matrices have columns that form orthonormal bases, and the "
"all-zero vector is not a unit vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora bien, $M$ ciertamente no es una matriz unitaria (salvo que $m=1,$ en "
"cuyo caso $\\Pi_0 = \\mathbb{I},$ lo que da $M = \\mathbb{I}$ en este caso "
"trivial), porque las matrices unitarias no pueden tener ninguna columna (ni "
"fila) que sea enteramente $0;$ las matrices unitarias tienen columnas que "
"forman bases ortonormales, y el vector cero no es un vector unitario.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, it is the case that the first $n$ columns of $M$ are orthonormal, and we get this from the assumption that $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ is a measurement.\n"
"To verify this claim, notice that for each $j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ the vector formed by column number $j$ of $M$ is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sin embargo, sí es cierto que las primeras $n$ columnas de $M$ son ortonormales, y esto lo obtenemos de la hipótesis de que $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ es una medición.\n"
"Para verificar esta afirmación, observa que para cada $j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ el vector formado por la columna número $j$ de $M$ es el siguiente:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle = M \\vert 0, j\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle = M \\vert 0, j\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that here we're numbering the columns starting from column $0.$ Taking "
"the inner product of column $i$ with column $j$ when "
"$i,j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ gives\n"
msgstr ""
"Nota que aquí estamos numerando las columnas a partir de la columna $0.$ "
"Tomando el producto interno de la columna $i$ con la columna $j$ cuando "
"$i,j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ obtenemos\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_i \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert i\\rangle\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1} \\vert l \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle k \\vert l \\rangle \\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle i \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\vert j \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & i = j\\\\\n"
"0 & i\\neq j,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_i \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert i\\rangle\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1} \\vert l \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle k \\vert l \\rangle \\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle i \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\vert j \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & i = j\\\\\n"
"0 & i\\neq j,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "which is what we needed to show.\n"
msgstr "que es lo que necesitábamos demostrar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, because the first $n$ columns of the matrix $M$ are orthonormal, we "
"can replace all of the remaining zero entries by some different choice of "
"complex number entries so that the entire matrix is unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Por lo tanto, dado que las primeras $n$ columnas de la matriz $M$ son "
"ortonormales, podemos reemplazar todas las entradas cero restantes por "
"alguna otra elección de entradas de números complejos de modo que la matriz "
"completa sea unitaria.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we're given the matrices $\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1},$ we can compute "
"suitable matrices to fill in for the blocks marked $\\fbox{?}$ in the "
"equation — using the Gram–Schmidt process — but it does not matter "
"specifically what these matrices are for the sake of this discussion.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si se nos dan las matrices $\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1},$ podemos calcular "
"matrices adecuadas para rellenar los bloques marcados con $\\fbox{?}$ en la "
"ecuación —usando el proceso de Gram–Schmidt— pero para los fines de esta "
"discusión no importa específicamente cuáles sean esas matrices.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally we can describe the measurement process: we first perform $U$ on the joint system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ and then measure $\\mathsf{Y}$ with respect to a standard basis measurement.\n"
"For an arbitrary state $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ of $\\mathsf{X},$ we obtain the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Finalmente podemos describir el proceso de medición: primero aplicamos $U$ sobre el sistema conjunto $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ y luego medimos $\\mathsf{Y}$ con respecto a una medición en la base estándar.\n"
"Para un estado arbitrario $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ de $\\mathsf{X},$ obtenemos el estado\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= M \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= M \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the first equality follows from the fact that $U$ and $M$ agree on their first $n$ columns.\n"
"When we perform a projective measurement on $\\mathsf{Y},$ we obtain each outcome $k$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"donde la primera igualdad se desprende del hecho de que $U$ y $M$ coinciden en sus primeras $n$ columnas.\n"
"Cuando realizamos una medición en la base estándar sobre $\\mathsf{Y},$ obtenemos cada resultado $k$ con probabilidad\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "in which case the state of $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ becomes\n"
msgstr "en cuyo caso el estado de $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ pasa a ser\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, $\\mathsf{Y}$ stores a copy of the measurement outcome and "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ changes precisely as it would had the projective measurement "
"described by $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ been performed directly on "
"$\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Así, $\\mathsf{Y}$ almacena una copia del resultado de la medición y "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ cambia exactamente como lo haría si la medición proyectiva "
"descrita por $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ se hubiera realizado "
"directamente sobre $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
